Rank distinct levels with DENSE_RANK, then aggregate the selected rank to one value. Bind k through the driver. A missing rank yields NULL rather than an arbitrary employee.

sql.solution:
WITH ranked AS (
 SELECT salary, DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS salary_level
 FROM employees WHERE salary IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT MAX(salary) AS kth_highest_salary FROM ranked WHERE salary_level = 3;
